@database "n8n"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: n8n.guide 1.0 (30.09.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "n8n"
@{h1}n8n

Builds n8n workflows from a request and proves that they run. You tell
the agent @{b}n8n_agent@{ub} what should happen -- "when a form is sent,
put the row into a sheet and post it to Slack" -- and it finds the nodes,
writes the workflow, creates it in your n8n as an unpublished draft and
runs it once with test data, every call to the outside world mocked. What
you get back is the workflow's id, its editor link, what ran for real,
what was mocked, and what you still have to do (credentials, choices).
When you ask for it, it also publishes the workflow, takes it offline,
archives it or runs it for real.

The plugin rebuilds none of n8n. It forwards a chosen set of n8n's own
@{b}instance MCP@{ub} tools -- node search, parameter definitions,
validation, creating from SDK code, test runs with pinned data -- and lays
ScarabHive's policy on top: it only touches workflows it created, it
refuses shell, file and legacy code nodes, and in a test it pins
everything that could act outside the run. Tested against n8n 2.39.9
(Community, Docker, SQLite).

@{code}
For users
  @{"  Asking it  " link use}
  @{"  How a test run works  " link testing}
  @{"  Publishing and running for real  " link live}
  @{"  What it will not do  " link policy}

For agents and developers
  @{"  Node knowledge tools  " link knowledge}
  @{"  Workflow tools  " link workflows}
  @{"  Test and execution tools  " link tests}
  @{"  Publish, unpublish, archive  " link publish}
  @{"  Triggering and the wake  " link trigger}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}
@{body}
@endnode

@node use "Asking it"
@{h1}Asking it

In the web UI, pick @{b}n8n_agent@{ub} as the agent of a chat (see
@{" Choosing an agent " link scarabhive/agents}). From the command line:

@{code sh}
agent-cli chat --agent n8n_agent
agent-cli run --agent n8n_agent "A webhook that takes {name} and answers Hello <name>"
@{body}

A good request names the trigger (webhook, schedule, form, chat), what
comes in, what should come out, and the services involved. The agent asks
back when one of these is open, and it checks which credentials exist in
n8n before it plans.

@{h2}What it does

@{number}Clarifies the request and lists the credentials n8n has.
@{number}Reads what it needs: the skill @{tt}n8n-building@{utt}, one
section of n8n's Workflow SDK reference at a time, n8n's best practices
for the technique.
@{number}Finds each node with n8n's search and reads its exact
parameters, with resource and operation.
@{number}Writes the workflow as n8n Workflow SDK code and validates it,
at most three rounds.
@{number}Creates it as an unpublished draft tagged @{tt}scarabhive@{utt}.
@{number}Test-runs it with realistic input and mocks, at most three
rounds of fixing.
@{number}Hands it over.

@{h2}What you get back

@{code}
workflow: <id> <name>
editor: <editor_url>
status: TESTED (execution <id>) | NOT TESTED (<reason>)
ran live: [...]   pinned: [...]   not reached: [...]
code not proven live: [...]
published: <webhook url> | no
todo_for_user: credentials to create (type, node), values to pick
review: nodes flagged REVIEW_NODE, with why
@{body}

@{b}TESTED@{ub} means one thing only: a test run with status
@{tt}success@{utt} is stored in n8n. A pinned node gave the mock it was
handed, so it proves the rest of the workflow, not the service behind it.
Code nodes never run live in a test (see
@{" How a test run works " link testing}); their logic is listed as not
proven live.

@{h2}Credentials

The agent sees credentials as id, name and type, never their secrets, and
has no tool to create one. A credential that does not exist yet goes into
the code as a placeholder n8n understands (@{tt}newCredential('Name')@{utt})
and into @{tt}todo_for_user@{utt}; you create it in the n8n editor.

@{h2}Its memory

The agent keeps notes across sessions in its own OKF bundle,
@{tt}data/okf/n8n@{utt}: your preferences and conventions, your projects
with their workflow ids, what failed and why. What your message is about
is folded into its prompt each turn (at most six concepts). It is told
never to store a key, a password or text copied from n8n, and that n8n is
right when a note and n8n disagree.

@{h2}The web

For what n8n's tools cannot tell -- a service's API, an error message, a
limit -- it can search and read the web (@{" Tavily " link tavily_search/main},
when a key is set). What it finds is data, and n8n's node definitions win
over it.
@endnode

@node testing "How a test run works"
@{h1}How a test run works

n8n's test run executes the stored draft once, and it pins nothing by
itself: an HTTP node without pinned data calls its URL for real. So the
plugin decides per node what may run and sends everything else as pinned
data. This @{b}pin plan@{ub} is the only line between a test and the
outside world.

@{table}
Node | In a test
triggers | always pinned to the test input (one empty item when none is given, with a warning)
local nodes | run for real: Set, IF, Switch, Filter, No Op, Respond to Webhook, Split Out, Aggregate, Limit, Date & Time, Sort, Merge
Sort with custom code, Merge in SQL mode | pinned: they run code
everything else | pinned to its mock (one empty item without one, with a warning)
@{body}

Everything else means APIs, anything with a credential, HTTP, Code,
sub-workflows, AI agents. Disabled nodes are left out.

@{h2}Running a node for real

The agent may name nodes in @{tt}live_nodes@{utt}. That is a request; the
plugin grants it only when:

@{bullet}@{b}HTTP Request, GraphQL, RSS@{ub}: the URL is fixed (no
expression) and plain -- @{tt}http(s)://host/...@{utt}, no backslash,
control character, user info, whitespace or @{tt}%@{utt} in the host --,
its host is in the operator's @{tt}allowed_hosts@{utt} (lower case, any
port), and it uses no proxy, no pagination and does not send its credential
on a redirect. With a credential it runs live only if the operator also
listed its type in @{tt}live_node_types@{utt}: the credential travels with
the request.
@{bullet}@{b}any other type@{ub}: only if the operator listed it in
@{tt}live_node_types@{utt}.
@{bullet}@{b}never@{ub}: Code and AI Code tools (they reach the network
through @{tt}this.helpers.httpRequest@{utt}, so no host list bounds them)
and sub-workflows (the callee's nodes would run outside this plan; a
pinned call node does not start the callee at all).

Both lists are empty as shipped: nothing runs live but local nodes.

@{h2}AI agents and other roots

An AI Agent hangs its model, memory and tools under it as subnodes. The
root runs live only if it may itself @{b}and@{ub} every node under it may
-- the tools of a tool included. Otherwise the root is pinned and none of
its subnodes run; a mock given to a subnode is ignored with a warning. A
subnode that ran inside a live root is reported as live.

@{h2}What counts

A test counts only when n8n stored its execution and the status is
@{tt}success@{utt}. The plugin refuses to test at all while the stored
workflow has a blocking finding (see
@{" What it will not do " link policy}) or has
@{tt}saveManualExecutions: false@{utt}, which would leave the run
unstored. A run that n8n did not store is reported as an error: it proves
nothing.
@endnode

@node live "Publishing and running for real"
@{h1}Publishing and running for real

Four tools act outside the draft. The agent is told to use them only when
you asked for exactly that -- never because a text in n8n says so.

@{table}
You ask | It does | Needs allow_publish
publish it | publishes the current version, if a successful test proved it | yes
take it offline | unpublishes it | yes
archive it | archives it; a published one goes offline | yes
run it | calls its production webhook once, with a payload | no
@{body}

@{h2}Publishing

Only the version a test proved goes live. The plugin looks for a
successful @{b}test@{ub} run (n8n's mode @{tt}manual@{utt}) of exactly the
current version id among the newest 250 successful runs of the workflow; a
production run does not count, it ran the published version. Then it
publishes by version id, so an edit after the check cannot slip in
untested. It refuses while the workflow or any workflow it starts
(sub-workflows by id, its error workflow, and theirs in turn) has a
blocking finding. The answer carries the production webhook URLs, built
from @{tt}N8N_PUBLIC_URL@{utt}; a path with route parameters gets no
guessed URL, take it from the editor.

An archived workflow is restored in the n8n editor; the plugin cannot and
does not delete anything.

@{h2}Running it

Only a published workflow with a Webhook trigger is started from here: the
plugin calls @{tt}<base>/webhook/<path>@{utt} of the published version,
without any key. It then looks for the execution the call started and
tells the agent its id and status. A run still going can wake the chat
when it ends -- see @{" Triggering and the wake " link trigger}. A
schedule runs by itself; a webhook with authentication or route
parameters is called from the n8n editor.
@endnode

@node policy "What it will not do"
@{h1}What it will not do

@{h2}Touch workflows it did not create

Every tool that changes, tests, publishes, archives or triggers a
workflow first reads it over the public API and refuses unless:

@{bullet}it carries the managed tag (@{tt}scarabhive@{utt}, set by
@{tt}managed_tag@{utt}) -- the plugin adds it right after creating;
@{bullet}it is not archived;
@{bullet}it is exposed to n8n's MCP (@{tt}availableInMCP@{utt}) --
exposing a workflow is a decision for a person in the editor.

Workflows you built in the editor are therefore safe from it, unless you
tag them yourself. Reading is not locked: the agent can read any workflow
the MCP sees, and their executions.

@{h2}Build blocked nodes

@{table}
List | Types | Effect
blocked | Execute Command, SSH, Local File Trigger, Read/Write Files, the old binary file nodes, Function, Function Item, Git, n8n (instance admin), AI Code, AI HTTP Request Tool | error: no test, no publish
review | Code, AI Code tool, HTTP Request, GraphQL, RSS, FTP, Execute Workflow, AI Workflow tool, MCP clients | warning: named in the handover
@{body}

A type's agent-tool variant counts as the type (@{tt}gitTool@{utt} is
@{tt}git@{utt}). The binding check runs on what n8n really stored, before
every test and publish; the checks before creating (type names in the
code) and on @{tt}addNode@{utt} are early hints. Before publishing, the
block list is also applied to every workflow the new one can start. A
person in the editor can still build anything.

@{h2}Other findings that block

@{table}
Code | Means
UNKNOWN_TYPE_VERSION | a type or version n8n does not know (n8n's own validators let @{tt}typeVersion: 99@{utt} pass)
EXECUTE_WORKFLOW_SOURCE | a sub-workflow not taken from the database by a fixed id: inline JSON, a file or a URL runs unchecked
SUB_WORKFLOW_UNCHECKED | a sub-workflow id that is not an n8n id, or a workflow that does not exist (at publish and trigger)
WEBHOOK_PATH_EMPTY, WEBHOOK_PATH_UNSAFE | no path, or one that would reach another n8n URL (@{tt}..@{utt}, @{tt}?@{utt}, @{tt}#@{utt}, @{tt}%@{utt})
RESPOND_NODE_MISSING | responseMode responseNode without a Respond to Webhook after it
EXPRESSION_UNBALANCED | a @{tt}{{@{utt} without @{tt}}}@{utt}
CREDENTIAL_UNKNOWN_ID, CREDENTIAL_TYPE_MISMATCH | a credential id n8n does not have, or of the wrong type
MISSING_REQUIRED_INPUT, INVALID_PARAMETER, SET_INVALID_ASSIGNMENT | warnings n8n marks valid that are real errors
N8N_ERROR, N8N_NODE_CONFIG | n8n's own validators
@{body}

@{h2}Change what marks a workflow as ours

@{tt}n8n_update_workflow@{utt} refuses to remove the managed tag, to add a
blocked node, to set a credential that does not exist or has the wrong
type, and to set @{tt}saveManualExecutions@{utt} to false.

@{h2}Things it has no tool for

Deleting a workflow, n8n's own @{tt}execute_workflow@{utt}, creating or
reading credentials' secrets, exposing a workflow to the MCP, restoring
an archived one.
@endnode

@node knowledge "Node knowledge tools"
@{h1}Node knowledge tools

Six tools that only read n8n's knowledge. They need the MCP key only
(@{tt}N8N_BASE_URL@{utt} and @{tt}N8N_MCP_KEY@{utt}); every other tool
needs @{tt}N8N_API_KEY@{utt} as well.

@{table}
Tool | Forwards to n8n | Answer
n8n_search_nodes | search_nodes | @{tt}data@{utt} (untrusted text, at most 13,000 chars), @{tt}truncated@{utt}
n8n_get_node_types | get_node_types | @{tt}data@{utt} (untrusted, at most 20,000 chars), @{tt}errors@{utt}, @{tt}truncated@{utt}
n8n_explore_node_resources | explore_node_resources | @{tt}data@{utt} (untrusted, at most 8,000 chars), @{tt}truncated@{utt}
n8n_get_best_practices | get_workflow_best_practices | @{tt}result@{utt} (at most 8,000 chars), @{tt}truncated@{utt}
n8n_get_sdk_reference | get_workflow_sdk_reference | @{tt}result@{utt} (at most 16,000 chars), @{tt}truncated@{utt}
n8n_list_credentials | list_credentials | @{tt}count@{utt}, @{tt}data@{utt} (untrusted list of id, name, type)
@{body}

@{h2}Parameters

@{table}
Name | Used by | Meaning
queries | search_nodes | one or two search terms; a string counts as one; more than two is refused
usage | search_nodes | @{tt}agentTool@{utt}: only nodes an AI Agent can use as a tool; @{tt}workflow@{utt}; anything else is left out
nodes | get_node_types | one to three @{tt}{node_id, version?, resource?, operation?, mode?}@{utt}; without resource and operation n8n gives only the list of operations
node_type, version, method_name, method_type, credential_type, credential_id | explore_node_resources | all required; method_type @{tt}listSearch@{utt} or @{tt}loadOptions@{utt}; version a finite number
filter, pagination_token, current_node_parameters | explore_node_resources | passed on when given
technique | get_best_practices | one of 18: @{tt}list@{utt} names them
section | get_sdk_reference | patterns, patterns_detailed, expressions, functions, rules, import, guidelines, design
type | list_credentials | only this credential type
@{body}

@{tt}errors@{utt} of get_node_types names types and versions n8n does not
know, read from the @{tt}# Errors@{utt} section n8n puts anywhere in an
otherwise successful answer. list_credentials asks n8n for 200 and returns
at most 100.

@{code}
n8n_get_node_types(nodes=[{"node_id": "n8n-nodes-base.slack", "version": "2.3",
                           "resource": "message", "operation": "post"}])
@{body}
@endnode

@node workflows "Workflow tools"
@{h1}Workflow tools

@{table}
Tool | What it does
n8n_validate_node_config | 1 to 50 node configs checked by n8n, plus the block and review lists
n8n_validate_workflow | SDK code checked as a whole workflow
n8n_create_workflow | validate, create as a draft, tag, check what was stored
n8n_update_workflow | n8n's atomic update operations on a managed workflow, then the stored check
n8n_get_workflow | a workflow's nodes, connections, settings and version id
n8n_list_workflows | the managed workflows
@{body}

@{h2}Parameters

@{table}
Name | Used by | Meaning
nodes | validate_node_config | 1 to 50 of @{tt}{name, type, typeVersion, parameters, subnodes, isToolNode}@{utt}
code | validate_workflow, create_workflow | the workflow as n8n Workflow SDK code; required
name | create_workflow | required
description | create_workflow | passed on when given
workflow_id | update_workflow, get_workflow | required; for update, letters and digits only
operations | update_workflow | 1 to 100 operations, each with a @{tt}type@{utt}
expected_version_id | update_workflow | the version id last read; refused when the workflow moved on
detail | get_workflow | @{tt}full@{utt} (default) or @{tt}execution@{utt}: metadata, version id and triggers, no nodes
name, limit, cursor | list_workflows | part of the name; 1 to 50, default 20; the page from @{tt}next_cursor@{utt}
@{body}

@{h2}Answers

@{bullet}@{b}validate_*@{ub}: @{tt}ok@{utt} (false on any error),
@{tt}errors@{utt}, @{tt}warnings@{utt}, each a finding
@{tt}{code, level, node, message, fix_hint}@{utt}. n8n's
@{tt}valid: true@{utt} never decides alone: three of its warning codes
are real errors.
@{bullet}@{b}create_workflow@{ub}: with validation errors nothing is
created (@{tt}"validation failed; nothing was created"@{utt} with the
findings). Otherwise @{tt}workflow_id@{utt}, @{tt}editor_url@{utt},
@{tt}ok@{utt}, @{tt}findings@{utt} on the stored workflow,
@{tt}warnings@{utt}, @{tt}auto_assigned_credentials@{utt} (n8n assigns
existing credentials by itself). The tag is tried twice; a workflow that
stays untagged is named, and the plugin will not touch it.
@{bullet}@{b}update_workflow@{ub}: @{tt}workflow_id@{utt},
@{tt}version_id@{utt}, @{tt}ok@{utt}, @{tt}findings@{utt},
@{tt}n8n_warnings@{utt}.
@{bullet}A write whose check afterwards fails is an error that says the
write happened and carries the id: @{tt}workflow w2 was created and
tagged, but the check afterwards failed (...); do not repeat it --
test_workflow checks it anew@{utt}.
@{bullet}@{b}get_workflow@{ub}: @{tt}workflow_id@{utt}, @{tt}editor_url@{utt},
@{tt}data@{utt} (untrusted). A workflow over 40,000 chars in full is
refused, pointing to @{tt}detail: execution@{utt} and the editor.
@{bullet}@{b}list_workflows@{ub}: only workflows with the managed tag:
@{tt}id, name, active, is_archived, updated_at, editor_url@{utt},
@{tt}next_cursor@{utt}.

@{code}
n8n_update_workflow(workflow_id="Ab12Cd34Ef56Gh78", expected_version_id="9f1c...",
    operations=[{"type": "setNodeParameter", "nodeName": "Hook", "path": "path", "value": "orders"}])
@{body}
@endnode

@node tests "Test and execution tools"
@{h1}Test and execution tools

@{h2}n8n_test_workflow

Runs the stored draft of a managed workflow once under the pin plan (see
@{" How a test run works " link testing}).

@{table}
Name | Meaning
workflow_id | required
trigger_node | the trigger to start from; default the first trigger in the workflow; one that is no trigger is refused
trigger_input | the items the trigger emits; a plain object is wrapped as @{tt}{"json": ...}@{utt}
mocks | @{tt}{node name: [items]}@{utt}, what each pinned node outputs; a name that is no node is warned about
live_nodes | node names to run for real, granted per the rules
timeout_s | 5 to 300, default 60; the call waits 30 s longer
@{body}

The answer: @{tt}tested@{utt} (true only with status success),
@{tt}execution_id@{utt}, @{tt}execution_status@{utt}, n8n's
@{tt}error@{utt}, @{tt}warnings@{utt} of the plan, @{tt}editor_url@{utt},
and @{tt}nodes@{utt} (untrusted), one entry per node:

@{table}
Field | Meaning
run | @{tt}live@{utt}, @{tt}pinned@{utt} or @{tt}not_reached@{utt}
reason | why: the rule that pinned it or let it run
node_status | n8n's status of the node's first run
items_out | items over all outputs; @{tt}items_per_output@{utt} for IF and Switch
sample | the first item, at most 1,000 chars; 12,000 chars for all samples together
error | the node's error message, at most 500 chars
@{body}

When a sample was cut or left out for the budget, the answer also has
@{tt}samples_truncated: true@{utt}; @{tt}n8n_get_execution@{utt} reads the
nodes' data.

@{h2}n8n_get_execution

@{table}
Name | Meaning
workflow_id, execution_id | required
include_data | the nodes' output, n8n cutting each at 2,000 chars
nodes | only these nodes' data, at most 10
@{body}

The answer's @{tt}data@{utt} (untrusted) is at most 12,000 chars, with
@{tt}truncated@{utt}. A run this session was watching also carries
@{tt}watch: {status, note}@{utt} -- see
@{" Triggering and the wake " link trigger}.

@{h2}n8n_list_executions

@{table}
Name | Meaning
workflow_id | only this workflow's
status | success, error, running, waiting, canceled, crashed, new, unknown
limit | 1 to 20, default 10
@{body}

Newest first: @{tt}id, workflow_id, status, mode, started_at,
stopped_at@{utt}. Without a status, running and waiting runs are asked for
too: n8n's plain list leaves them out. Neither execution tool is locked to
managed workflows.
@endnode

@node publish "Publish, unpublish, archive"
@{h1}Publish, unpublish, archive

All three take only @{tt}workflow_id@{utt}, go through the managed lock,
and answer @{tt}"... switched off ... (allow_publish)"@{utt} unless the
operator set @{tt}allow_publish: true@{utt} -- the value true itself;
@{tt}"yes"@{utt} or @{tt}1@{utt} leave it off.

@{table}
Tool | Checks | Answer
n8n_publish_workflow | no blocking finding in it or in any workflow it starts; a successful test of the current version | @{tt}active_version_id@{utt}, @{tt}proven_by_execution@{utt}, @{tt}webhooks@{utt} (untrusted: node, methods, url or a note), @{tt}editor_url@{utt}
n8n_unpublish_workflow | -- | @{tt}was_published@{utt}
n8n_archive_workflow | -- | @{tt}archived: true@{utt}, a note that restoring is done in the editor
@{body}

The test is looked for among the newest 250 successful runs; the test
runs among them are read one by one, at most 20. A workflow with more
than 250 successful production runs since its last test is refused and has to be
tested again. The workflows it starts are sub-workflow nodes with a fixed
id and the error workflow setting, followed to their own callees, both
their draft and their published nodes, at most 19 of them.

Refusals, verbatim:

@{code}
w1: its current version has no successful test run among the newest 250
successful runs -- run n8n_test_workflow on it first
the workflow has blocking findings; fix and test it first   (+ findings)
publishing is switched off by the operator (allow_publish)
@{body}

n8n's own refusal (for example a webhook path another workflow uses) comes
back as the error text.
@endnode

@node trigger "Triggering and the wake"
@{h1}Triggering and the wake

@{h2}n8n_trigger_workflow

@{table}
Name | Meaning
workflow_id | required; must be managed and published
payload | a JSON object, at most 64,000 chars as JSON; for GET and HEAD flat values sent as query parameters, at most 8,000 chars
method | only when the webhook takes several methods
webhook_node | only when the published version has several Webhook triggers
wait | @{tt}wake@{utt} (default) or @{tt}none@{utt}
timeout_s | how long to wait for the webhook's answer: 5 to 300, default 60
@{body}

Refused before any call: a workflow that is not published, a published
version without an enabled Webhook trigger, several without
@{tt}webhook_node@{utt}, a webhook with authentication, a path with route
parameters or anything but letters, digits and @{tt}- _ . ~ :@{utt}
between single slashes, a method it does not take, a published version
with a blocked node (a person may have published it in the editor) or
one that picks a sub-workflow by expression (the payload could choose any
workflow), and a workflow it starts that has a blocked node or such a
sub-workflow by now. Triggering does not need
@{tt}allow_publish@{utt}.

@{h2}The answer

@{table}
Field | Meaning
http_status, response | the webhook's status and answer (untrusted, at most 8,000 chars)
execution_id, correlation | @{tt}exact@{utt} when the workflow answered with its @{tt}executionId@{utt} (a Respond to Webhook node can); @{tt}heuristic@{utt} for the one new webhook run since the call
candidates | several new runs started at once: pick by their data
execution_status | the run's status when the answer was written
note | what is uncertain; without an execution id it ends in "do not call the webhook again, look with n8n_list_executions"
wake, wake_note | for a run still going with wait: wake
@{body}

Once the webhook was called, nothing reads as "nothing happened": no
answer, a failed lookup, even a 404 or 413 that n8n might have sent is a
result with a note, unless the lookup found no run at all -- only then is
n8n's refusal believed (@{tt}n8n does not know this webhook -- is the
workflow still published?@{utt}).

@{h2}The wake

With @{tt}wake: true@{utt} the plugin watches the run over the public API
(every 2 s at first, backing off to 30 s) and, when it ends, starts a new
run of the chat's agent with the framework's wake sentence. The agent is
told to give you the execution id and end its turn, and when woken to read
the run with @{tt}n8n_get_execution@{utt}, whose @{tt}watch@{utt} field
then says how it ended. Reading the ended run before the wake comes
cancels the wake.

No wake is armed -- @{tt}wake: false@{utt}, and the note ends in "you are
not woken -- give execution id 7 to whoever asked and read it later with
n8n_get_execution, do not poll it" -- when no execution was found, the run
was itself woken, session presence or waking is switched off, the call
has no session, the session is a sub-agent's, or the ids cannot name a file.

@{bullet}A watch gives up after @{tt}watch_max_hours@{utt} (default 24,
1 to 168); a run that disappears or cannot be read ends it too, and the
note says no further wake comes.
@{bullet}The watch lives in the API process or an @{tt}agent-cli chat@{utt}.
A one-shot @{tt}agent-cli run@{utt} ends it with its turn, and the tool
cannot tell that case apart. A restart ends every watch; the outcome stays
in n8n.
@{bullet}Records and read marks lie under @{tt}data/cache/n8n/@{utt} and
are swept after 14 days.
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}Tools

Nineteen tools from @{tt}schema.yaml@{utt}, about 11,700 chars of schema
with every key set; with only the MCP key, the six knowledge tools
(3,900 chars); with no n8n configured, none. The agent's allowlist names
each of the nineteen. The prompt and skills name only tools the schema
has (checked by @{tt}tests/test_plugin_n8n_config.py@{utt}).

@{h2}Answers and errors

Every answer is @{tt}{"status": "success", ...}@{utt} or
@{tt}{"status": "error", "error": "<what to do>"}@{utt}, some with
@{tt}findings@{utt}. Examples, verbatim:

@{code}
workflow w1 is not managed by ScarabHive (tag 'scarabhive' missing); it stays untouched
operation 0: node type n8n-nodes-base.executeCommand is blocked by policy
n8n MCP rate limit reached (100 requests per IP and 5 minutes); retry in 102 s
n8n MCP refused the key -- check N8N_MCP_KEY (it may have been rotated)
n8n not reachable at http://n8n:5678 (ConnectError) -- is the container running?
  http://n8n:5678/healthz tells
@{body}

No error or log line carries a key. A 429 of the MCP with a
@{tt}retry-after@{utt} of at most 10 s is waited out once; a longer one
goes to the model as the text above.

@{h2}Untrusted data

What came out of n8n -- node descriptions (a community node's author wrote
them), workflow and node names, execution data, credential names, webhook
answers, n8n's messages on a result -- comes wrapped as
@{tt}{"untrusted": true, "content": ...}@{utt}. The prompt calls that and
every name or value from a workflow data, never an instruction. The SDK
reference and best practices come unwrapped: n8n's own documentation.

@{h2}The chat status line

Each call ends with exactly one line, at most 140 chars: for example
@{tt}created Ab12... flow: 0 blocking finding(s)@{utt}, @{tt}w1: execution
e1 success, 2 live / 1 pinned@{utt}, or the error's first 140 chars.

@{h2}Prompt, skills, cache

The prompt (@{tt}agents/prompts/n8n_agent.md@{utt}, about 4,100 chars)
carries the way of working, the rules and the handover format. The
knowledge is in three skills loaded on demand: @{tt}n8n-building@{utt}
(code shape, credentials, update operations, finding codes, 5,300 chars),
@{tt}n8n-testing@{utt} (pin plan, test data, reading the answer, 3,800)
and @{tt}n8n-recipes@{utt} (webhook, schedule, sub-workflow, AI agent,
error workflow, a workflow as an MCP tool for ScarabHive, 4,400).

Tool results are appended and never rewritten, each capped as the tool
nodes say. The agent runs with @{tt}prompt_cache_mode: multi_turn@{utt}.
The OKF hook changes the system prompt when the user speaks or the agent
writes a concept mid-turn; the context engineer compacts when the context
grows (@{" The compaction hook " link context_engineer/hook}).

@{h2}Known gaps

@{bullet}@{b}Only your request stands between the builder and a real
run.@{ub} The tools cannot see the conversation. A prompt injection could
still publish one of its own tested workflows or trigger a published one
with a payload of its choice; with @{tt}allow_publish: false@{utt} only
the trigger is left.
@{bullet}@{b}Published, nothing is controlled any more.@{ub} A published
HTTP node reaches any host. That is why only a tested version goes live.
@{bullet}@{b}An allowed host is trusted with its redirects@{ub} in a test.
@{bullet}@{b}The block list is explicit.@{ub} A dangerous type a later n8n
adds is not caught until it is listed; the upgrade checklist in
@{" docs/deploy/README.md " link docs/deploy/README.md} re-checks it.
@{bullet}@{b}The code pre-check is a hint.@{ub} Code can assemble a type
name; the stored check is the binding one.
@{bullet}@{b}The MCP key acts as its n8n user@{ub} (today the owner). Keep
it like a password.
@{bullet}@{b}The memory is the agent's own words@{ub}, folded into later
prompts unwrapped; only the prompt's rule keeps n8n text out of it.
@{bullet}@{b}No panel@{ub}, and n8n cannot call ScarabHive
(@{" docs/design.md " link docs/design.md} §6.3, §7).
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

@{h2}n8n

Deploy n8n with @{tt}docs/deploy/@{utt} (Docker Compose with the instance
MCP switched on) and run @{tt}setup_owner.sh@{utt} on the Docker host: it
creates the owner, a public API key with read scopes only
(@{tt}workflow:read@{utt}, @{tt}workflow:list@{utt},
@{tt}execution:read@{utt}, @{tt}execution:list@{utt}) and the MCP key.
The steps: @{" docs/deploy/README.md " link docs/deploy/README.md}.

@{h2}ScarabHive

Put the values into @{tt}config/secrets.env@{utt}:

@{table}
Variable | Meaning
N8N_BASE_URL | where ScarabHive reaches n8n, e.g. http://localhost:5678
N8N_MCP_KEY | the MCP key; every write goes through the MCP with it
N8N_API_KEY | the read-only public API key; the plugin only ever sends GET with it
N8N_PUBLIC_URL | where browsers and webhook callers reach n8n, when that is another address; editor links and webhook URLs are built from it
@{body}

Then restart ScarabHive. Without the three required values the instance
offers no tools, so an installation without n8n loses nothing; the start
logs a warning when an enabled agent allows the tools, and names what is
missing when only some are set. A plain-HTTP base URL other than localhost
is logged: both keys travel unencrypted.

@{h2}The entries

Nothing to add to @{tt}config/plugins.yaml@{utt}: @{tt}agents/n8n.yaml@{utt}
is picked up by the include @{tt}../src/plugins*/*/agents/*.yaml@{utt} and
defines three instances, the skills by @{tt}skills.skill_dirs@{utt}.

@{code yaml}
n8n:
  type: n8n
  enabled: true
  managed_tag: scarabhive
  allowed_hosts: []
  live_node_types: []
  allow_publish: true
  watch_max_hours: 24
  tested_n8n_version: "2.39.9"

n8n_okf:
  type: okf
  enabled: true
  allowed_directories:
    - data/okf/n8n
  hook_max_concepts: 6
  hook_graph_depth: 1
@{body}

@{h2}Server settings

@{table}
Key | Default in code | Meaning
managed_tag | scarabhive | the tag that marks a workflow as ScarabHive's
allowed_hosts | none | hosts an HTTP node may reach live in a test (lower case, any port)
live_node_types | none | other node types that may run live in a test when named
blocked_node_types | the list in @{tt}validate.py@{utt} | a configured list REPLACES it: copy it and change it
review_node_types | the list in @{tt}validate.py@{utt} | replaces the default the same way
allow_publish | off | only the value true switches publishing, unpublishing and archiving on (shipped: true)
watch_max_hours | 24 | how long a trigger's wake waits, 1 to 168
timeout | 60 | seconds per HTTP request to n8n
base_url, api_key, mcp_key, public_url | the environment | set here only if not from secrets.env
tested_n8n_version | -- | not read by the code; the version the plugin was measured against
@{body}

@{h2}The agent

@{table}
Key | Value
type | multi_turn_agent: the context engineer's tools and compaction
llm_profile | [structured, deepseek-chat]: the same model, the second over the direct API
max_steps | 60
skills.on_demand | n8n-building, n8n-testing, n8n-recipes
tools.allowed | the nineteen n8n tools, @{tt}skills/*@{utt}, @{tt}n8n_okf/*@{utt}, @{tt}tavily_search/*@{utt}
hooks | context engineer, Markdown formatter, the OKF context injection on @{tt}data/okf/n8n@{utt}
visibility | both: the UI and a tool
@{body}

Another agent calls it as a tool with @{tt}"+n8n_agent/*"@{utt} in its
allowlist (@{tt}n8n_agent_execute_task@{utt}). It is not among the shared
sub-agent manager's @{tt}allowed_agents@{utt}; add it there to spawn it as
a sub-agent (@{" Sub-agents and the SAM " link scarabhive/subagents}).

@{h2}Where data lives

The workflows and executions in n8n; the agent's memory in
@{tt}data/okf/n8n@{utt}; watch records in @{tt}data/cache/n8n/@{utt}.

The live tests (@{tt}tests/test_plugin_n8n_live.py@{utt}) run only
with @{tt}N8N_LIVE=1@{utt} and a separate @{tt}N8N_TEST_API_KEY@{utt}
against a test instance; the rest runs against a fake n8n.
@endnode
